{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6418a024-c3a4-4814-8a47-877c8ee710e8",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Stock Movement)",
    "description": "Inventory module \u2014 Stock Movement (`/api/v1/inventory/stock-movements`). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory (create-stock-movement.dto.ts, stock-movement.response.dto.ts).\n\nAPPEND-ONLY / IMMUTABLE (Ch.39.5, STM-002) \u2014 there is NO update or delete endpoint for Stock Movement at all (index.ts only mounts POST/GET, never PUT/DELETE for /stock-movements). This collection therefore contains no PUT/DELETE requests and no 'Historical Immutability' 404 probe either (unlike Exchange Rate's own collection) \u2014 the route is simply never mounted, by design, and there is nothing further to demonstrate about it here.\n\nMANUAL FIXTURE GAP \u2014 read before running (applies to every request in this collection): `productId` is the Business layer's own contract for Stock Movement (a real, in-module numeric bigint FK, not a `productUuid` resolved to one) \u2014 there is NO endpoint anywhere that returns a Product's internal numeric id (06_DATABASE_STANDARDS.md PK-003 forbids ever serializing it \u2014 `GET /products/:uuid` only ever returns `uuid`). `{{productId}}` defaults to \"1\", a plausible first-row id on a freshly-seeded local dev DB \u2014 before running this collection, manually verify it against your local MySQL (e.g. `SELECT id FROM products WHERE uuid = '<real product uuid>'`) and replace {{productId}} with the real value. A stale/wrong {{productId}} makes every request fail with a NotFound-style domain error \u2014 a sign of a stale fixture, not proof this collection is broken. `{{warehouseUuid}}`/`{{otherWarehouseUuid}}` similarly default to \"\" and must be filled in from real Warehouses (create them via the sibling `Warehouse.postman_collection.json`) before running TRANSFER-shaped requests, which need two distinct warehouses. Same treatment the repo already gives other manual-fixture gaps (Authentication hardcodes `tenantId=1`; Warehouse needs a manual `branchUuid`).\n\nDOCUMENTED SCOPE LIMITATION: creating a Stock Movement also atomically updates the real Stock on-hand quantity for the affected Warehouse/Product pair (STM-001, create-stock-movement.service.ts). This collection only verifies the Stock Movement resource's own HTTP response shape \u2014 it does not chain into the Stock collection's own GET to assert the downstream Stock side-effect (that would require cross-collection chaining, out of scope here; treated as a documented limitation rather than silently worked around).\n\nEvery route requires `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` AND `X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}`. No Authorization header at all fails jwt-auth.middleware.ts before this module's own request validation ever runs \u2014 401 `AUTH_MISSING_TOKEN`. A missing/malformed `X-Tenant-Id` header, or a malformed request body, is rejected as 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. STM-003's per-movementType required-warehouse rule is enforced by create-stock-movement.service.ts and surfaces as 422 `INV_STOCK_MOVEMENT_INVALID_WAREHOUSE` (StockMovementMissingRequiredWarehouseError, domain-error-http-mapping.ts). Business errors not individually mapped fall back to 422 `INV_DOMAIN_ERROR`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
